      },
      "lineNbr": 45,
      "author": {
        "id": 1530208
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-08-27T17:26:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As with CMA, isn\u0027t it possible to also have multiple carveout heaps? So, shouldn\u0027t we handle the carveout heap IDs in a similar fashion?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 45,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 45,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "a0d1635f56297fdb96ca5617b62e2bf05554c685",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "415d0b66_176be854",
        "filename": "include/uapi/linux/ion.h",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 45,
      "author": {
        "id": 1108565
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-08-27T19:08:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We could, but I wonder if its worth adding all that complexity if none of the Android code is going to use them.\n\nFor now the assumption is there can be multiple CMA heaps and only 1 of other staandard types of heaps that Android system can / will talk to.\nHowever, if you have the need to add additional carveout heaps, they can be of a different type and specify their own heap id? (that reminds me, I am not handling this case, so will fix that too).",
      "parentUuid": "0b708375_a455ee30",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 45,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 45,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "a0d1635f56297fdb96ca5617b62e2bf05554c685",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "367241f2_89aeca73",
        "filename": "include/uapi/linux/ion.h",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 45,
      "author": {
        "id": 1530208
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-08-27T19:29:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I suppose we can, but IMO, that seems rather awkward, because the heaps are, by definition, carveout heaps; they just need different IDs.\n\nIt seems strange to have the ideas of heap type and heap IDs so tightly coupled as they are here, because these aren\u0027t really types anymore (i.e. it makes sense to have multiple heaps of type CMA, but the way we\u0027re doing that is by having a heap of type CMA, type CMA + 1, type CMA + 2, etc, which doesn\u0027t make much sense?)",
      "parentUuid": "415d0b66_176be854",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 45,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 45,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "a0d1635f56297fdb96ca5617b62e2bf05554c685",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "66ce800f_71affa4f",
        "filename": "include/uapi/linux/ion.h",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 45,
      "author": {
        "id": 1108565
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-08-28T05:22:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Oh I agree. I don\u0027t like the type \u003d\u003d id thing one bit. I haven\u0027t though through to see if there are any user space implications of this yet.\n\nIt probably makes the ion_heap_assign_ids() bigger, but I guess I\u0027ll do that now.",
      "parentUuid": "367241f2_89aeca73",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 45,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 45,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "a0d1635f56297fdb96ca5617b62e2bf05554c685",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
